<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech IPB  lowers base rate 50 bps.</title>
<headline>Czech IPB  lowers base rate 50 bps.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prague-based Investicni a Postovni Banka a.s.  said on Wedneday that it would lower its base lending rate on new credit by 50 basis points on August 1 to 20.0 percent.</p>
<p>It said the base rate for credits granted before the beginning of 1995 would fall 50 basis points to 24.0 percent. It left its prime rate unchanged at 12.9 percent.</p>
<p>The move is concurrent with rate reductions at other major Czech banks, and follows a general downward trend in rates on the interbank market.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
